            <ArticleTitle>Avoiding being dragged away: finding egg cases of Schroederichthys bivius (Chondrichthyes: Scyliorhinidae) associated with benthic invertebrates.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>248-253</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jfb.13490</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Egg cases of the narrowmouthed catshark Schroederichthys bivius were recorded entangled with sponges, corals and tubeworms at different sites in the south-west Atlantic Ocean. This work sheds light on the importance of benthic invertebrates in the life cycle of oviparous chondrichthyan species.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 The Fisheries Society of the British Isles.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
